{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_fsrcrys3ojd64zn6g7j46mzv7roicmzirwrx3bunlevmwprrvaea","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four phases done, with one real bug found and fixed.\n\n## What the library is\n`c_src` is a single function — `void driver(char c)` — that resets the locale to `\"C\"` and prints 14 lines classifying `c` via `<ctype.h>` and printing its case conversions. One exported symbol total.\n\n## Phase A — artifacts (`translation/`)\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — 1 C symbol (`driver`); exported by the Rust `.so` under the exact name. No stubs, no skipped modules.\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — 9 rows. Grepping the C found **zero** explicit error paths (no `return`, no `assert`, no checks — the file has no branches at all), so the table is derived from the implicit rejection surface: NUL output via `%c`, negative `char` table indices, `-128`/`127`/`-1` boundaries, out-of-range `int` passed to the `char` parameter (the FFI equivalent of an invalid enum value), and hostile/failing `setlocale` state.\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — 23 rows: one per ctype equivalence class the tables actually distinguish, plus sign-of-`char`, exhaustive all-256, repeat calls, caller-installed locales, interleaved C/Rust calls, and wide-`int` argument shapes.\n\n## Phases B–D — tests\n`tests/diff.rs` (34 cases) loads **both** `.so`s through `libloading` and calls only the exported `driver` symbol, capturing each implementation's `printf` bytes by redirecting fd 1, then comparing byte-for-byte. `run_verification.sh` builds the C ground truth, enumerates feature combos from `Cargo.toml` (there are none — default is the only configuration, confirmed mechanically), and runs everything in **both debug and release** with a `nm -D` symbol diff. Result: symbol diff empty, 34/34 passing in both profiles.\n\n## Bug found and fixed\nRows C22/E6/E7 exposed a **release-only SIGSEGV**: passing an `int` that doesn't fit in `char` (e.g. `0x1234_5641`) crashed the Rust `.so`, while the C printed the low byte's results. `ctype.rs` guarded a 384-entry table with `if c >= -128 && c < 256`, but since the argument arrives as an ABI-sign-extended `i8`, the optimizer legally folded the guard away and indexed with the full-width register — an out-of-bounds read. Debug happened to keep the check, so `-O0` testing alone would never have seen it. Fixed by keying the tables on the `char`'s byte (`[c_int; 256]`), making every lookup structurally in bounds at any optimization level and reproducing the C's truncation exactly; behavior is unchanged across `-128..=255` because the `\"C\"` locale's negative and `128..=255` halves are empty.\n\nTwo things worth flagging:\n- I confirmed the suite isn't vacuously green by mutation-testing it: flipping `isblank` for `\\t` failed 5 rows, and altering `toupper('a')` failed 6.\n- `cargo test` alone does not build a cdylib-only lib target, so the harness was initially loading a stale *release* `.so` while reporting a debug run. It now fails loudly if the profile's artifact is missing (or honors `DRIVER_RUST_SO`), and the test target uses `harness = false` with a sequential runner, because libtest's multi-threaded progress writes to the same fd 1 the capture hijacks and corrupted comparisons under default parallelism.\n\n`c_src/` was not modified (only the instructed `build/` directory was added)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":802,"cache_read_input_tokens":93404,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":802,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a986d300-6bfb-4a34-8cc4-9236e56c9507","uuid":"39278ef6-710e-4115-b91a-06b53c510190","timestamp":"2026-08-28T14:53:03.424Z"}
